# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps a locally built
# node_modules out of the image.
#
# Without this, the generated Dockerfile's `COPY . /app/.` ships your machine's
# node_modules into the container. `npm ci` then tries to delete that directory
# before reinstalling, and on the builder's overlay filesystem the delete fails
# with EBUSY on node_modules/.cache. Never copying it in avoids the problem
# entirely, and the build gets faster because the context shrinks by 700 MB.

node_modules
.next
out
build

# Runtime data belongs on a mounted volume, never baked into an image.
data

.git
.gitignore
*.log
.DS_Store
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
